  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 206 PM MDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nFor much of next week we don't see too much of a difference \ncompared to this week, with nearly daily chances (at least 15%) \nof showers/storms. On Monday we start the week on the back side \nof an upper level ridge with southwest flow aloft and a 850-700 \nmb area of high pressure over the Four Corners region. \nThroughout the day, most mid to long range guidance is favoring \na weak cold front pushing south across the area, which should \nmake the environment more favorable for showers and storms \nduring the evening to potentially overnight hours. In regards to\nthe severe potential, so far CAPE remains a concern as a \nlimiting factor with GFS guidance favoring less than 500 J/kg \nover our Colorado counties. Winds shear is still somewhat \nfavorable with 25-30 kts of surface-3 km shear and ~30 kts of \neffective shear. With precipitable water values around 1 in, we \ncould see more rain showers than storms if any activity does \ndevelop and move into the area.\n\nTuesday through Thursday, weak shortwaves in the mid to upper \nlevels of the atmosphere will work to strengthen a near-surface \ntrough on the lee side of the Rockies. These shortwaves may help\nwith the rain/storm chances as we move into the middle of the \nweek. So far guidance is favoring more isolated/pop-up style \nactivity, but confidence in showers or storms developing is \nfairly low (<20%). Models, including the NBM, are leaning more \ntowards chances tapering off during this time frame.\n\nAs the precipitation chances go down, the temperatures are \nexpected to increase throughout next week. Monday and Tuesday we\nare looking at highs in the upper 80s to upper 90s, with the \ntemperatures \"coolest\" west of the Colorado border. Wednesday \nand Thursday temperatures are expected to warm up a few degrees \nmore with highs in the 90s and possibly reaching the triple \ndigits east of Highway 83. Overnight lows will be mild in the \n60s to lower 70s.",
